"""Known-photo damage annotations for the dummy predictor.

The dummy predictor has no real computer vision — everywhere else it just
invents plausible-looking random detections. For the handful of demo photos
that show genuine, visually verified damage (see
scripts/sample_photos/SOURCE.md), we instead recognize the photo and return
accurate, hand-annotated bounding boxes matching what's actually visible in
it. Recognition uses a small perceptual fingerprint (16x16 grayscale
downsample) so it survives JPEG re-compression and the plate-number overlay
stamped in the corner by the demo seed script — not a real classifier, just
enough to say "is this one of our known reference photos."

Any image that doesn't match one of these falls back to the predictor's
normal random behavior, which is the honest thing to do for a genuinely
unknown photo.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import numpy as np
import cv2

